  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224461/assets/df0c2e8a1af51ce0765ca2689f2ee1043d940d2abe2f8f18616786ace1fb18ac.png)\n\nThe volume of the cube above is $8\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.$ What is the length of its sides?",
  "worked_solution": "Since the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt[3]{V}=\\sqrt[3]{8}=2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side is $2\\,\\text{ft}.$",
